	(text "Not fitted by default. With the VGA dongle the sync source is the DE-15's VSYNC (pin 14) and GND (pin 10).\nWith the HDMI dongle there is no analogue sync to tap: bring frame sync out on a spare PRO GPIO in this\nrepo's firmware instead, or leave the tap off and time frames from /INT alone.\nU2 translates a 3.3 V source to 5 V. HCT thresholds (VIH 2.0 V) make 3.3 V an unambiguous high;\nthe Nano's own VIH of 3.0 V does not. A5 = PC5 = PCINT13, timestamped inside its pin-change interrupt."
		(exclude_from_sim yes)
		(at 78.74 241.3 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "d37b17ee-a427-4a3a-9640-44bf8d3d2ead")
	)
	(text "THE BUS HARNESS"
		(exclude_from_sim yes)
		(at 62.23 55.88 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.54 2.54)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "f918a7ba-6ceb-44f8-98b7-f660d95a7e75")
	)
	(text "The PICO9918 PRO sits in the TMS9918A's 40-pin DIP position on a breadboard or a DIP-40 socket.\nAn Arduino Nano drives its four ports; the Mac drives the Nano over USB serial. Every connection\nbelow is a jumper wire. Nothing is fabricated."
		(exclude_from_sim yes)
		(at 62.23 58.42 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "409e5f5b-2874-4548-976b-5d96d7c17ddd")
	)
	(text "PREPARING THE PRO"
		(exclude_from_sim yes)
		(at 62.23 69.85 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.778 1.778)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "810d5265-e679-40e5-9dc8-f5b4804ee97a")
	)
	(text "MDE1 (pin 11) has no pin fitted: MODE1 is not a TMS9918 signal, so the PRO ships with\nthat pad bare. Solder one 0.1\" male header pin into it. Without it, port B ($9C02/$9C03)\nis unreachable — on the bench and in the AC6502 alike. No other modification is needed.\n\nPin 33 (+5V) is LEFT UNCONNECTED. The PRO runs from its own USB-C, which also carries the\ndebug link to the Mac. The Nano runs from its own USB. Only ground is common: tie the Nano's\nGND to the PRO's pin 12 through the breadboard's ground rail.\n\nBack up the stock flash before anything else: picotool save, in BOOTSEL, kept outside the repo."
		(exclude_from_sim yes)
		(at 62.23 72.39 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "79bc3c5a-dc19-400f-b792-60a938ebc415")
	)
	(text "MODE1:MODE = CPU A1:A0. They select the port:\n  0 0  $9C00  data          0 1  $9C01  address / register\n  1 0  $9C02  port B data   1 1  $9C03  port B command"
		(exclude_from_sim yes)
		(at 198.12 72.39 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "ae116cb0-acde-46de-a053-581ee7eb5f09")
	)
	(text "PORT DECODE"
		(exclude_from_sim yes)
		(at 198.12 69.85 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.778 1.778)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "99dfa2b3-0a34-4c50-a17d-6027f1aff307")
	)
	(text "TI numbers this bus backwards: CD0 is the MOST significant bit and CD7 the LEAST.\npico9918 samples GPIO 14 (CD7) as bit 0. Get this wrong and every byte arrives bit-reversed.\nR1-R8 are 220 Ω series protection only — they limit the current if a harness bug drives the\ndata lines while the PRO is driving them. The socket side of the PRO is 5 V logic, so the Nano\nneeds no level shifting: a 74HC245 drives out and a 5 V-tolerant 74LVC245 receives."
		(exclude_from_sim yes)
		(at 93.98 183.52 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "25c21baf-f20c-4fa8-b7ea-507c926466df")
	)
	(text "D0 and D1 carry the USB serial link to the Mac at 1,000,000 baud\n(500,000 is the exact fallback). The 328P's 16 MHz clock hits both\nrates exactly; the USB bridge and its macOS driver must too.\n\nD0/D1 are taken by that link, and PB6/PB7 and PC6 hold the crystal\nand reset, so the 328P has no free 8-bit port. Data is split: six\nbits on PORTD, two on PORTB. Control stays on PORTC alone, so each\nstrobe edge is still a single port write.\n  On a write, both data ports are set before /CSW falls.\n  On a read, both are sampled while /CSR is low, one instruction\n  (62.5 ns) apart, and the PRO holds the bus throughout.\n\nD8 = PB0 = ICP1, the 328P's ONLY input-capture pin. /INT must land\nhere: Timer 1 timestamps its edges to 62.5 ns.\n\nD11-D13 stay free. D13's on-board LED is the harness's status light."
		(exclude_from_sim yes)
		(at 272 120.65 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "7bb52469-0d36-435b-90f8-738c48c0e560")
	)
	(text "THE NANO"
		(exclude_from_sim yes)
		(at 272 118.11 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.778 1.778)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "e41abe49-986d-4af0-be79-b0c0b3e16ae1")
	)
	(text "VIDEO"
		(exclude_from_sim yes)
		(at 272 176.53 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.778 1.778)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "26bba4eb-e7a0-4ca5-841d-4f8f3ec5f3b0")
	)
	(text "The PRO's video leaves by the FFC cable to its dongle, and never\ntouches this harness:\n  PRO → FFC → HDMI dongle → HDMI capture card → Mac\n'vdpctl grab' saves a PNG through ffmpeg -f avfoundation.\nCapture is never the pass/fail oracle — the snapshot over the debug\nlink is. Capture proves what a snapshot cannot see: sync lock, DAC\nbit order, line doubling, a picture that stays stable under load."
		(exclude_from_sim yes)
		(at 272 179.07 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "029b1ce5-daf0-42b7-b5b2-cd408ccdd7ff")
	)
	(text "SIGNAL TIMING"
		(exclude_from_sim yes)
		(at 272 205.74 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.778 1.778)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "df72c114-0a0a-4771-8602-41c4f6579808")
	)
	(text "The harness runs three profiles, set from the host:\n  6502-1mhz   ~500 ns strobes, accesses ≥ 4 µs apart\n  6502-2mhz   ~250 ns strobes, accesses ≥ 2 µs apart\n  fastest     as fast as the 328P can drive the pins\nStrobe width, data setup and hold can also be set directly, for\nmargin sweeps. The harness never asserts /CSR and /CSW together,\nand tri-states both data ports before /CSR falls."
		(exclude_from_sim yes)
		(at 272 208.28 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "f81703ce-50f9-44c5-85a7-6dfea04106f5")
	)
	(text "See docs/BENCH.md for the wiring table, the harness protocol and the bring-up order."
		(exclude_from_sim yes)
		(at 272 232.41 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "cc34c6b5-56b1-446b-8752-171480eae66f")
	)
